Getting Started with Unitree G1 using Unitree MuJoCo


****************************
Software

This assumes that you are using Ubuntu 20.04 and have installed the necessary C++ software by following 
https://github.com/unitreerobotics/unitree_mujoco


**************************
Running for the first time
1)
Make a copy of this folder

2)
Open a terminal, say terminal 1
Navigate to the folder

3) 
cmake .


***************************

Now we will run the simulator

4) IN the folder unitree_mujoco/simulate 
drop the config.yaml file 

- sets G1
- set elastic band = 1


5)
Open another terminal, say terminal 2 and navigate to the folder unitree_mujoco/simulate/build 
./unitree_mujoco 


********************

Now we will run the controller
6) Go to terminal 1 


make
./stand_g1

We will modify two of the reference angles

NOTE: Alternately, put these lines in another file, say run_stand_g1

chmod +x run_stand_g1
./run_stand_g1


You can quit the controller by pressing ctrl+c and re-running it as many times. You dont need to start the simulator again.


